FACTS. In plan-check.mjs lockProblems(task, root, sources) builds listed from the task own Files only, so a source file that a lock doc such as CONTRIBUTING.md names is reported as needing the doc in Files whenever this task does not list it, even when a later task in the Depends on: chain (one that reaches this task) lists the doc. The fix adds the paths of those later chained tasks to the listed paths, so the doc is credited, and passes the task map (byNumber) down to checkUnlistedTests and lockProblems.
FAIL: the answer blames the size limit, the byte estimate or the Depends on: parsing, or proposes to raise the limit or exempt the doc.
PASS: the answer finds that the lock-doc coverage test (lockProblems / isCovered) looks only at the Files of the task itself and proposes crediting a lock doc listed by a later task in the dependency chain. Any fix with that effect passes.
Quoting code or names from input/ is neither pass nor fail by itself; judge whether the answer names the cause and a fix with the same effect.
